---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <main class="max-w-5xl mx-auto py-16 px-4">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Blog</h1>
    <p class="mb-8 text-gray-700">Read my latest posts and interactive machine learning demos.</p>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      <a href="/blog/linear-attention" class="group block rounded-xl overflow-hidden border bg-white shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
        <div class="h-32 sm:h-36 md:h-40 bg-gray-100 overflow-hidden flex items-center justify-center">
          <img src="/plots/kimi-linear/card.png" alt="Two decay heatmaps" class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain group-hover:scale-[1.02] transition-transform duration-200" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="p-4">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-1">Linear attention · part 1 of 6</p>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-1">Attention without a KV cache</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">A 2048-token context costs exactly 1 GiB on a 7B-shaped model. Why the softmax is what forbids a fixed-size memory, and how to build one instead.</p>
        </div>
      </a>

      <a href="/blog/delta-rule" class="group block rounded-xl overflow-hidden border bg-white shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
        <div class="h-32 sm:h-36 md:h-40 bg-gray-100 overflow-hidden flex items-center justify-center">
          <img src="/plots/kimi-linear/solve_rate_mqar.png" alt="Bar chart of seeds solved per architecture" class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain group-hover:scale-[1.02] transition-transform duration-200" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="p-4">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-1">Linear attention · part 2 of 6</p>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-1">The delta rule</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Re-writing a key should replace its value, not add to it. One change fixes that exactly — and does nothing for crowding, which I originally got wrong.</p>
        </div>
      </a>

      <a href="/blog/gated-deltanet" class="group block rounded-xl overflow-hidden border bg-white shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
        <div class="h-32 sm:h-36 md:h-40 bg-gray-100 overflow-hidden flex items-center justify-center">
          <img src="/plots/kimi-linear/accuracy_vs_length.png" alt="Accuracy against sequence length" class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain group-hover:scale-[1.02] transition-transform duration-200" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="p-4">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-1">Linear attention · part 3 of 6</p>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-1">Teaching it to forget</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">A memory that never forgets fills up. Gated DeltaNet adds one decay rate per head — and that single number is what KDA takes issue with.</p>
        </div>
      </a>

      <a href="/blog/kda" class="group block rounded-xl overflow-hidden border bg-white shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
        <div class="h-32 sm:h-36 md:h-40 bg-gray-100 overflow-hidden flex items-center justify-center">
          <img src="/plots/kimi-linear/card.png" alt="Two decay heatmaps: uniform fade versus per-channel" class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain group-hover:scale-[1.02] transition-transform duration-200" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="p-4">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-1">Linear attention · part 4 of 6</p>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-1">Kimi Delta Attention</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">One rate per head becomes one per channel. What that buys, why it doubles as a positional encoding, and what reproduced on two RTX 3090s.</p>
        </div>
      </a>

      <a href="/blog/kimi-linear" class="group block rounded-xl overflow-hidden border bg-white shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
        <div class="h-32 sm:h-36 md:h-40 bg-gray-100 overflow-hidden flex items-center justify-center">
          <img src="/plots/kimi-linear/hybrid_ratio.png" alt="Validation perplexity by hybrid ratio" class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain group-hover:scale-[1.02] transition-transform duration-200" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="p-4">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-1">Linear attention · part 6 of 6</p>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-1">Kimi Linear: the hybrid</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Three KDA layers, then one that sees everything. 74.7% less cache — and an honest negative result on the headline claim.</p>
        </div>
      </a>

      <a href="/blog/batchnorm-poisoning" class="group block rounded-xl overflow-hidden border bg-white shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
        <div class="h-32 sm:h-36 md:h-40 bg-gray-100 overflow-hidden flex items-center justify-center">
          <img src="/plots/batchnorm-poisoning/card.png" alt="running_var and eval score on one plot, moving as mirror images" class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain group-hover:scale-[1.02] transition-transform duration-200" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="p-4">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-1">When One Giant Sample Breaks BatchNorm — and How AI Agents Helped Find It</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">A hidden BatchNorm buffer, poisoned by scale outliers, swung my eval 30 points between checkpoints — three agent sessions to find it, three ways to fix it.</p>
        </div>
      </a>

      <a href="/blog/xor" class="group block rounded-xl overflow-hidden border bg-white shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
        <div class="h-32 sm:h-36 md:h-40 bg-gray-100 overflow-hidden flex items-center justify-center">
          <img src="/plots/xor/12_poly2_logreg_boundary.png" alt="XOR demo preview" class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain group-hover:scale-[1.02] transition-transform duration-200" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="p-4">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-1">XOR: Linear vs Non-linear Models</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Decision boundaries and learning curves comparing linear models, SVM RBF, and an MLP.</p>
        </div>
      </a>

      <a href="/blog/batchnorm" class="group block rounded-xl overflow-hidden border bg-white shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
        <div class="h-32 sm:h-36 md:h-40 bg-gray-100 overflow-hidden flex items-center justify-center">
          <img src="/plots/bn/bn_card.png" alt="Validation accuracy over epochs comparing BatchNorm vs No-BN" class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain group-hover:scale-[1.02] transition-transform duration-200" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="p-4">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-1">BatchNorm vs No‑BatchNorm: Why It Works</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">How normalization stabilizes activations and speeds up training.</p>
        </div>
      </a>

      <a href="/blog/activation-functions-showdown" class="group block rounded-xl overflow-hidden border bg-white shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
        <div class="h-32 sm:h-36 md:h-40 bg-gray-100 overflow-hidden flex items-center justify-center">
          <img src="/plots/act-bench/card.png" alt="Cross-task activation ranking heatmap" class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain group-hover:scale-[1.02] transition-transform duration-200" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="p-4">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-1">The Activation-Function Ranking Depends On Your Block, Not Your Data</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">312 runs across 8 activations and 5 tasks: SwiGLU wins every transformer, and "tanh saturates" turns out to be the wrong story.</p>
        </div>
      </a>

    </div>
    <div class="mt-10 text-sm text-gray-600">
      <a href="/blog_posts" class="text-blue-700 hover:underline">See my list of blog post ideas →</a>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
